  "body": {
    "id": "thm:published-positive-preservation",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Whenever Algorithms 1--2 of Lee, Ghassami, and Shpitser return an identifying functional using only selector values in \\(H\\) and denominators supported on \\(\\mathcal C_H^{\\mathrm{adm}}(G^{+})\\), \\(\\operatorname{SA\\mbox{-}CS\\mbox{-}ID}\\) returns \\((F_H,\\mathcal D_H^{\\mathrm{den}},\\mathfrak D_H)\\) such that \\(O_H(\\theta)\\in\\mathfrak D_H\\) and \\(F_H\\{O_H(\\theta)\\}=T_{a,H}(\\theta)\\) for every \\(\\theta\\in\\Theta_H\\). Gate reinsertion makes the returned circuit and its required positive margins algebraically equal to the published derivation on the original expansion.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "H",
      "Cadm",
      "Gplus",
      "SACSID",
      "FH",
      "dH",
      "DH",
      "OH",
      "theta",
      "TH",
      "ThetaH"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:admissible-cell-interior",
      "lem:restricted-support-denominator-positivity",
      "lem:lgs-algorithm-soundness",
      "lem:nonresidual-progress",
      "lem:published-trace-scheduling",
      "thm:normalization-equivalence",
      "def:initial-token-compiler",
      "def:sa-csid-machine",
